---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#e9e2d2" />
    <title>Protocol — Itihāsa Atlas</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="subpage protocol-page">
      <header class="subnav">
        <a class="wordmark wordmark--ink" href="/">
          ITIHĀSA <span>ATLAS</span>
        </a>
        <nav aria-label="Product navigation">
          <a href="/#atlas">ATLAS</a>
          <a href="/verse-lens">VERSE LENS</a>
          <a href="/pathfinder">PATHFINDER</a>
          <a aria-current="page" href="/protocol">
            PROTOCOL
          </a>
        </nav>
      </header>
      <section class="protocol-page__intro" data-od-id="protocol-intro">
        <p class="label">PUBLIC METHOD / 2026</p>
        <h1>What this atlas will not pretend to know.</h1>
        <p>
          An epic with many recensions cannot be made more trustworthy by hiding its
          disagreements. This is the publication protocol behind every page.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="protocol-list" data-od-id="protocol-list">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h2>Name the edition</h2>
          <p>
            Every source note identifies its working edition, parva, adhyāya and verse
            where available.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h2>Keep attestation visible</h2>
          <p>
            Critical Edition, vulgate and regional retellings are data on the record—not a
            footnote after the fact.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h2>Publish only reviewed verse work</h2>
          <p>
            Draft Sanskrit, transliteration and translation remain explicitly provisional
            until a named reviewer signs off.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
